IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa27-part43.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 43 "Transparency obligations and related matters" (ss 1265 to 1273),
-- lines 18053-18348 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART IS. Each of ss 1265 to 1271 is an instruction to insert provisions into Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000
-- (FSMA): ss 89A to 89G, 89H to 89J, 89K to 89N, 89O, 90A and 90B, and 100A. The instruction itself ("In Part 6 of the Financial Services and
-- Markets Act 2000 ... insert") amends another Act: machinery, inert in the coverage table (reason 2), as are s 1266(2) (a transitional
-- saving), s 1272 (Schedule 15), and the empty s 1273. The text inserted is the Act's own words in the range, and where it states a rule a
-- person in the seat can be asked about, it is encoded here, under the Companies Act section number with the FSMA label as a sub-label:
-- `s 1270 FSMA 90A(3) ...`. The rule-making powers of the competent authority and the Treasury (ss 89A to 89G, 89O, 90B) are machinery, inert.
-- (Fork F-H in NOTES.md states the policy and the other reading, under which all of Part 43 would be inert.)
--
-- BORROWED TERMS. The Transparency Obligations Directive (2004/109/EC), Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 and the FSMA's own definitions are not among
-- the sources: each borrowed answer is an INPUT, MAYBE BOOLEAN where it is a term of art (NOTHING passes through as NOTHING).
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words ("means", "if", "only if",
-- "unless", "does not affect", "must not be greater"); NOTHING the text does not decide. A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1265 The transparency obligations directive
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18057 | “the transparency obligations directive” means Directive 2004/109/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council relating to the harmonisation of transparency requirements in relation to information about issuers whose securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market;.
@ref s 1265 The transparency obligations directive: FSMA s 103(1) (src:18057-18057)
GIVEN `the instrument is Directive 2004/109/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council relating to the harmonisation of transparency requirements in relation to information about issuers whose securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1265 FSMA 103(1) the instrument is the transparency obligations directive` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Directive 2004/109/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council relating to the harmonisation of transparency requirements in relation to information about issuers whose securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the transparency obligations directive” means Directive 2004/109/EC"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1266 Transparency rules (FSMA ss 89A to 89G)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18079 | (5) Rules under this section are referred to in this Part as “transparency rules”.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89A(5) Transparency rules (src:18079-18079)
GIVEN `the rules were made under section 89A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89A(5) the rules are transparency rules` MEANS
    IF `the rules were made under section 89A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Rules under this section are referred to in this Part as “transparency rules”" does not say that no other rules are

-- src:18087 | (3) In this Part “voteholder information” in respect of voting shares means information relating to the proportion of voting rights held by a person in respect of the shares.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89B(3) Provision of voteholder information (src:18087-18087)
GIVEN `the information relates to the proportion of voting rights held by a person in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89B(3) the information is voteholder information` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to the proportion of voting rights held by a person in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voteholder information” in respect of voting shares means information relating to the proportion of voting rights held by a person in respect of the shares"

-- The same wording appears in s 89B(6) and s 89D(3): lines 18095-18098 and 18126-18129 differ only in the subsection number "(6)" and "(3)"
-- (checked with diff), so one function answers both and the second is a thin wrapper that cites its own lines.
-- src:18095 | (6) For this purpose there is a “notifiable change” in the proportion of voting rights held by a person when the proportion changes—
-- src:18096 | (a) from being a proportion less than a designated proportion to a proportion equal to or greater than that designated proportion,
-- src:18097 | (b) from being a proportion equal to a designated proportion to a proportion greater or less than that designated proportion, or
-- src:18098 | (c) from being a proportion greater than a designated proportion to a proportion equal to or less than that designated proportion.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89B(6) Provision of voteholder information: "notifiable change" (src:18095-18098)
GIVEN `the proportion before the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion after the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the designated proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89B(6) there is a notifiable change in the proportion of voting rights held by a person` MEANS
    IF       (`the proportion before the change` LESS THAN `the designated proportion` AND `the proportion after the change` AT LEAST `the designated proportion`)
          OR (`the proportion before the change` EQUALS `the designated proportion` AND `the proportion after the change` GREATER THAN `the designated proportion`)
          OR (`the proportion before the change` EQUALS `the designated proportion` AND `the proportion after the change` LESS THAN `the designated proportion`)
          OR (`the proportion before the change` GREATER THAN `the designated proportion` AND `the proportion after the change` AT MOST `the designated proportion`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is a “notifiable change” in the proportion of voting rights held by a person when the proportion changes" (a "when" condition counts as "where": the ruling of 2026-11-05)

-- src:18099 | (7) In subsection (6) “designated” means designated by the rules.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89B(7) Provision of voteholder information: "designated" (src:18099-18099)
GIVEN `the proportion is designated by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89B(7) the proportion is designated` MEANS
    IF `the proportion is designated by the rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“designated” means designated by the rules"

-- src:18126 | (3) For this purpose there is a “notifiable change” in the proportion of voting rights held by a person when the proportion changes—
-- src:18127 | (a) from being a proportion less than a designated proportion to a proportion equal to or greater than that designated proportion,
-- src:18128 | (b) from being a proportion equal to a designated proportion to a proportion greater or less than that designated proportion, or
-- src:18129 | (c) from being a proportion greater than a designated proportion to a proportion equal to or less than that designated proportion.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89D(3) Notification of voting rights held by issuer: "notifiable change" (src:18126-18129)
GIVEN `the proportion before the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion after the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the designated proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89D(3) there is a notifiable change in the proportion of voting rights held by a person` MEANS
    `s 1266 FSMA 89B(6) there is a notifiable change in the proportion of voting rights held by a person`
        `the proportion before the change` `the proportion after the change` `the designated proportion`

-- src:18130 | (4) In subsection (3) “designated” means designated by the rules.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89D(4) Notification of voting rights held by issuer: "designated" (src:18130-18130)
GIVEN `the proportion is designated by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89D(4) the proportion is designated` MEANS
    `s 1266 FSMA 89B(7) the proportion is designated` `the proportion is designated by the rules`

-- ---- s 89F: interpretation ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18138 | (a) the voting rights in respect of any voting shares are the voting rights attached to those shares,
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(a) Transparency rules: interpretation (src:18138-18138)
GIVEN `the voting rights are those attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(a) the voting rights are the voting rights in respect of the voting shares` MEANS
    IF `the voting rights are those attached to the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the voting rights in respect of any voting shares are the voting rights attached to those shares"

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) either answer holds` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            IF y THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:18139 | (b) a person is to be regarded as holding the voting rights in respect of the shares—
-- src:18140 | (i) if, by virtue of those shares, he is a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive;
-- src:18141 | (ii) if, and to the extent that, he is entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise those voting rights in one or more of the cases mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of the transparency obligations directive;
-- src:18142 | (iii) if he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares and is an Article 13 instrument, and
-- src:18143 | (c) a person holds a “comparable instrument” in respect of voting shares if he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument in relation to the shares which has similar economic effects to an Article 13 instrument (whether or not the financial instrument results in an entitlement to acquire the shares).
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) Transparency rules: when a person is regarded as holding the voting rights (src:18139-18143)
GIVEN `by virtue of those shares he is a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he is entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise those voting rights in one or more of the cases mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of the transparency obligations directive` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial instrument is an Article 13 instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) the person is regarded as holding the voting rights in respect of the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) either answer holds`
                (`s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) either answer holds`
                    `by virtue of those shares he is a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive`
                    `he is entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise those voting rights in one or more of the cases mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of the transparency obligations directive`)
                (IF `he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares`
                 THEN `the financial instrument is an Article 13 instrument`
                 ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN JUST g THEN
        IF g THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): each limb is introduced by "if" (the lawyer-flag reading (a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no, clause by clause)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Articles 2.1(e), 10(a) to (h) and 13 of the transparency obligations directive

-- src:18143 | (c) a person holds a “comparable instrument” in respect of voting shares if he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument in relation to the shares which has similar economic effects to an Article 13 instrument (whether or not the financial instrument results in an entitlement to acquire the shares).
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(c) Transparency rules: "comparable instrument" (src:18143-18143)
GIVEN `he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument in relation to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial instrument has similar economic effects to an Article 13 instrument (whether or not it results in an entitlement to acquire the shares)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(c) the person holds a comparable instrument in respect of the voting shares` MEANS
    IF `he holds, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument in relation to the shares` AND `the financial instrument has similar economic effects to an Article 13 instrument (whether or not it results in an entitlement to acquire the shares)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person holds a “comparable instrument” in respect of voting shares if he holds" (the lawyer-flag reading (a))

-- src:18145 | (3) For the purposes of sections 89A to 89G two or more persons may, at the same time, each be regarded as holding the same voting rights.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(3) Transparency rules: the same voting rights held by two persons (src:18145-18145)
GIVEN `the first person is regarded as holding the voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second person is regarded as holding the same voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(3) two or more persons may each be regarded as holding the same voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the first person is regarded as holding the voting rights` AND `the second person is regarded as holding the same voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "two or more persons may, at the same time, each be regarded as holding the same voting rights"

-- src:18147 | “Article 13 instrument” means a financial instrument of a type determined by the European Commission under Article 13.2 of the transparency obligations directive;
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) Transparency rules: "Article 13 instrument" (src:18147-18147)
GIVEN `the instrument is a financial instrument of a type determined by the European Commission under Article 13.2 of the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) the instrument is an Article 13 instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is a financial instrument of a type determined by the European Commission under Article 13.2 of the transparency obligations directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Article 13 instrument” means a financial instrument of a type determined by the European Commission"

-- src:18148 | “UK market” means a market that is situated or operating in the United Kingdom;
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) Transparency rules: "UK market" (src:18148-18148)
GIVEN `the market is situated or operating in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) the market is a UK market` MEANS
    IF `the market is situated or operating in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK market” means a market that is situated or operating in the United Kingdom"

-- src:18149 | “voting shares” means shares of an issuer to which voting rights are attached.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) Transparency rules: "voting shares" (src:18149-18149)
GIVEN `the shares are shares of an issuer to which voting rights are attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) the shares are voting shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are shares of an issuer to which voting rights are attached`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting shares” means shares of an issuer to which voting rights are attached"

-- src:18153 | (3) The competent authority may make public any information notified to the authority in accordance with transparency rules.
@ref s 1266 FSMA 89G(3) Transparency rules: the competent authority may make public (src:18153-18153)
GIVEN `the information was notified to the competent authority in accordance with transparency rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1266 FSMA 89G(3) the competent authority may make the information public` MEANS
    IF `the information was notified to the competent authority in accordance with transparency rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information notified to the authority in accordance with transparency rules"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1267 Competent authority's power to call for information (FSMA ss 89H to 89J)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(a) an issuer in respect of whom transparency rules have effect`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(b) a voteholder`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(c) an auditor of an issuer to whom this section applies or of a voteholder`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(d) a person who controls a voteholder`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(e) a person controlled by a voteholder`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(f) a director or other similar officer of an issuer to whom this section applies`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2)(g) a director or other similar officer of a voteholder or, where its affairs are managed by its members, a member of the voteholder`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) another kind of person`

-- src:18164 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:18165 | (a) an issuer in respect of whom transparency rules have effect;
-- src:18166 | (b) a voteholder;
-- src:18167 | (c) an auditor of—
-- src:18168 | (i) an issuer to whom this section applies, or
-- src:18169 | (ii) a voteholder;
-- src:18170 | (d) a person who controls a voteholder;
-- src:18171 | (e) a person controlled by a voteholder;
-- src:18172 | (f) a director or other similar officer of an issuer to whom this section applies;
-- src:18173 | (g) a director or other similar officer of a voteholder or, where the affairs of a voteholder are managed by its members, a member of the voteholder.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) Competent authority's power to call for information: the persons (src:18164-18173)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) another kind of person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to" the seven kinds, and the text does not say it applies to no others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18161 | (1) The competent authority may by notice in writing given to a person to whom this section applies require him—
-- src:18162 | (a) to provide specified information or information of a specified description, or
-- src:18163 | (b) to produce specified documents or documents of a specified description.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89H(1) Competent authority's power to call for information: the notice (src:18161-18163)
GIVEN `the competent authority has given the person a notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this section applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information or documents are reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the competent authority of functions conferred on it by or under sections 89A to 89G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89H(1) the person must provide the information or produce the documents` MEANS
    IF NOT `the competent authority has given the person a notice in writing`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The competent authority may by notice in writing given to a person to whom this section applies require him"
    ELSE IF NOT `the information or documents are reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the competent authority of functions conferred on it by or under sections 89A to 89G`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (3), "This section applies only to information and documents reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the competent authority of functions"
         ELSE CONSIDER `this section applies to the person`
              WHEN JUST p THEN
                  IF p THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person to whom this section applies"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the person is not one of the seven kinds in subsection (2), which the text does not say are the only ones

-- src:18175 | (4) Information or documents required under this section must be provided or produced—
-- src:18176 | (a) before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified, and
-- src:18177 | (b) at such place as may be specified.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89H(4) Competent authority's power to call for information: time and place (src:18175-18177)
GIVEN `the last day of the reasonable period specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the information was provided or the documents were produced` IS A DATE
      `the information was provided or the documents were produced at the place specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89H(4) the information was provided or the documents were produced as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the day the information was provided or the documents were produced` AT MOST `the last day of the reasonable period specified in the notice`
         AND `the information was provided or the documents were produced at the place specified in the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be provided or produced— (a) before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified, and (b) at such place as may be specified" (a period and a place fixed in the notice: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:18178 | (5) If a person claims a lien on a document, its production under this section does not affect the lien.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89H(5) Competent authority's power to call for information: lien (src:18178-18178)
GIVEN `the person claims a lien on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89H(5) the production of the document under this section affects the lien` MEANS
    IF `the person claims a lien on the document`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "its production under this section does not affect the lien"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person claims a lien on a document"

DECLARE `s 1267 FSMA 89I requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 1267 FSMA 89I(1) that information provided be in a form it reasonably requires`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89I(2)(a) that information provided be verified in a manner it reasonably requires`
    `s 1267 FSMA 89I(2)(b) that a document produced be authenticated in a manner it reasonably requires`

-- src:18180 | (1) The competent authority may require any information provided under section 89H to be provided in such form as it may reasonably require.
