`s 1267 FSMA 89I(5) the competent authority may require him to state where the document is` MEANS
    IF `a person who is required under section 89H to produce a document fails to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person who is required under section 89H to produce a document fails to do so, the competent authority may require him to state" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q9)

-- src:18194 | (1) The competent authority may require an issuer to make public any information provided to the authority under section 89H.
-- src:18195 | (2) If the issuer fails to comply with a requirement under subsection (1), the competent authority may, after seeking representations from the issuer, make the information public.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89J(1)-(2) Power to call for information: supplementary provisions (src:18194-18195)
GIVEN `the person is an issuer who has been required to make public information provided to the authority under section 89H` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89J(1) the competent authority may require the issuer to make public the information` MEANS
    IF `the person is an issuer who has been required to make public information provided to the authority under section 89H`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The competent authority may require an issuer to make public any information provided to the authority under section 89H"

@ref s 1267 FSMA 89J(2) Power to call for information: the competent authority makes it public (src:18195-18195)
GIVEN `the issuer fails to comply with a requirement under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority has sought representations from the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89J(2) the competent authority may make the information public` MEANS
    IF NOT `the issuer fails to comply with a requirement under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the issuer fails to comply with a requirement under subsection (1), the competent authority may" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q10)
    ELSE IF `the competent authority has sought representations from the issuer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the competent authority may, after seeking representations from the issuer, make the information public" (an "after" gate: listed, not flipped, in the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12)

-- src:18198 | “specified” means specified in the notice;
