-- src:18201 | (b) is treated as holding such rights by virtue of rules under section 89A(3)(b).
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89J(3) Power to call for information: "voteholder" (src:18199-18201)
GIVEN `the person holds voting rights in respect of voting shares for the purposes of sections 89A to 89G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is treated as holding such rights by virtue of rules under section 89A(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89J(3) the person is a voteholder` MEANS
    IF `the person holds voting rights in respect of voting shares for the purposes of sections 89A to 89G` OR `the person is treated as holding such rights by virtue of rules under section 89A(3)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voteholder” means a person who"

-- src:18207 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4)(b)—
-- src:18208 | (a) any rights of a person controlled by A, and
-- src:18209 | (b) any rights of a person acting on behalf of A or a person controlled by A,
-- src:18210 | are treated as held by A..
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89J(5) Power to call for information: rights treated as held by A (src:18207-18210)
GIVEN `A holds the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person controlled by A holds the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person acting on behalf of A or of a person controlled by A holds the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89J(5) the right is treated as held by A for the purposes of subsection (4)(b)` MEANS
    IF `A holds the right` OR `a person controlled by A holds the right` OR `a person acting on behalf of A or of a person controlled by A holds the right`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (4)(b)— (a) any rights of a person controlled by A, and (b) any rights of a person acting on behalf of A or a person controlled by A, are treated as held by A"

-- src:18202 | (4) For the purposes of those sections a person (“A”) controls another person (“B”) if—
-- src:18203 | (a) A holds a majority of the voting rights in B,
-- src:18204 | (b) A is a member of B and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the members of the board of directors (or, if there is no such board, the equivalent management body) of B,
-- src:18205 | (c) A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B, or
-- src:18206 | (d) A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B.
@ref s 1267 FSMA 89J(4) Power to call for information: "controls" (src:18202-18206)
GIVEN `A holds a majority of the voting rights in B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a member of B and the right to appoint or remove a majority of the members of the board of directors (or the equivalent management body) of B is held by A or treated as held by A under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1267 FSMA 89J(4) A controls B` MEANS
    IF       `A holds a majority of the voting rights in B`
          OR `A is a member of B and the right to appoint or remove a majority of the members of the board of directors (or the equivalent management body) of B is held by A or treated as held by A under subsection (5)`
          OR `A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B`
          OR `A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (“A”) controls another person (“B”) if"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1268 Powers exercisable in case of infringement of transparency obligation (FSMA ss 89K to 89N)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18215 | (1) If the competent authority finds that an issuer of securities admitted to trading on a regulated market is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation, it may publish a statement to that effect.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(1) Public censure of issuer: the statement (src:18215-18215)
GIVEN `the issuer's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority finds that the issuer is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(1) the competent authority may publish a statement that the issuer has failed to comply` MEANS
    IF `the issuer's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` AND `the competent authority finds that the issuer is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the competent authority finds that an issuer of securities admitted to trading on a regulated market is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation, it may publish a statement" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q11)

-- src:18216 | (2) If the competent authority proposes to publish a statement, it must give the issuer a warning notice setting out the terms of the proposed statement.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(2) Public censure of issuer: the warning notice (src:18216-18216)
GIVEN `the competent authority proposes to publish a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(2) the competent authority must give the issuer a warning notice` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority proposes to publish a statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the competent authority proposes to publish a statement, it must give the issuer a warning notice" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:18217 | (3) If, after considering any representations made in response to the warning notice, the competent authority decides to make the proposed statement, it must give the issuer a decision notice setting out the terms of the statement.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(3) Public censure of issuer: the decision notice (src:18217-18217)
GIVEN `after considering any representations made in response to the warning notice, the competent authority decides to make the proposed statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(3) the competent authority must give the issuer a decision notice` MEANS
    IF `after considering any representations made in response to the warning notice, the competent authority decides to make the proposed statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, after considering any representations ..., the competent authority decides to make the proposed statement, it must give the issuer a decision notice" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:18218 | (4) A notice under this section must inform the issuer of his right to refer the matter to the Tribunal (see section 89N) and give an indication of the procedure on such a reference.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(4) Public censure of issuer: the notice must inform (src:18218-18218)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice under section 89K` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(4) the notice must inform the issuer of his right to refer the matter to the Tribunal` MEANS
    IF `the notice is a notice under section 89K`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice under this section"

-- src:18219 | (5) In this section “transparency obligation” means an obligation under—
-- src:18220 | (a) a provision of transparency rules, or
-- src:18221 | (b) any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(5) Public censure of issuer: "transparency obligation" (src:18219-18221)
GIVEN `the obligation is an obligation under a provision of transparency rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is an obligation under any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(5) the obligation is a transparency obligation` MEANS
    IF `the obligation is an obligation under a provision of transparency rules` OR `the obligation is an obligation under any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“transparency obligation” means an obligation under— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:18222 | (6) In relation to an issuer whose home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom, any reference to an applicable transparency obligation must be read subject to section 100A(2).
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89K(6) Public censure of issuer: home State (src:18222-18222)
GIVEN `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89K(6) any reference to an applicable transparency obligation is read subject to section 100A(2)` MEANS
    IF `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to an issuer whose home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom"

-- src:18224 | (1) This section applies to securities admitted to trading on a regulated market.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89L(1) Power to suspend or prohibit trading of securities: scope (src:18224-18224)
GIVEN `the securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89L(1) this section applies to the securities` MEANS
    IF `the securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to securities admitted to trading on a regulated market" (a scope limit with no "only": ruling "Periods, where and scope limits" (c); the name test of 2026-11-12 keeps it, fork F-P)

DECLARE `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) measure` IS ONE OF
    `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(a) suspend trading in the securities for a period`
    `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(b) prohibit trading in the securities`
    `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(c)(i) request the operator of the market to suspend trading for a period`
    `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(c)(ii) request the operator of the market to prohibit trading`

-- src:18225 | (2) If the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by an issuer, it may—
-- src:18226 | (a) suspend trading in the securities for a period not exceeding 10 days,
-- src:18227 | (b) prohibit trading in the securities, or
-- src:18228 | (c) make a request to the operator of the market on which the issuer's securities are traded—
-- src:18229 | (i) to suspend trading in the securities for a period not exceeding 10 days, or
-- src:18230 | (ii) to prohibit trading in the securities.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) Power to suspend or prohibit trading of securities: reasonable grounds for suspecting (src:18225-18230)
GIVEN `this section applies to the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      measure IS A `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) measure`
      `the number of days of the suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) the competent authority may take the measure` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies to the securities`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to securities admitted to trading on a regulated market"
    ELSE IF NOT `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by an issuer`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by an issuer, it may" (the name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-P: this function is named for a power, and JUST FALSE for an unmet gate would read as "may not")
         ELSE CONSIDER measure
              WHEN `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(a) suspend trading in the securities for a period` THEN
                  IF `the number of days of the suspension` AT MOST 10
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a period not exceeding 10 days"
              WHEN `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(b) prohibit trading in the securities` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(c)(i) request the operator of the market to suspend trading for a period` THEN
                  IF `the number of days of the suspension` AT MOST 10
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to suspend trading in the securities for a period not exceeding 10 days"
              WHEN `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2)(c)(ii) request the operator of the market to prohibit trading` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:18231 | (3) If the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a provision required by the transparency obligations directive has been infringed by a voteholder of an issuer, it may—
-- src:18232 | (a) prohibit trading in the securities, or
-- src:18233 | (b) make a request to the operator of the market on which the issuer's securities are traded to prohibit trading in the securities.
