GIVEN `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a provision required by the transparency obligations directive has been infringed by a voteholder of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89L(3) the competent authority may prohibit trading in the securities, or request the operator to prohibit it` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a provision required by the transparency obligations directive has been infringed by a voteholder of an issuer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a provision required by the transparency obligations directive has been infringed by a voteholder of an issuer, it may" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q12)

-- src:18234 | (4) If the competent authority finds that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed, it may require the market operator to prohibit trading in the securities.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89L(4) Power to suspend or prohibit trading of securities: a finding of infringement (src:18234-18234)
GIVEN `the competent authority finds that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89L(4) the competent authority may require the market operator to prohibit trading in the securities` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority finds that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the competent authority finds that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed, it may require the market operator to prohibit trading" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q13)

-- src:18235 | (5) In this section “transparency obligation” means an obligation under—
-- src:18236 | (a) a provision contained in transparency rules, or
-- src:18237 | (b) any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive.
-- src:18238 | (6) In relation to an issuer whose home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom, any reference to an applicable transparency obligation must be read subject to section 100A(2).
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89L(5)-(6) Power to suspend or prohibit trading of securities: definition and home State (src:18235-18238)
GIVEN `the obligation is an obligation under a provision contained in transparency rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is an obligation under any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
