    `s 1268 FSMA 89K(5) the obligation is a transparency obligation`
        `the obligation is an obligation under a provision contained in transparency rules`
        `the obligation is an obligation under any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive`

GIVEN `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89L(6) any reference to an applicable transparency obligation is read subject to section 100A(2)` MEANS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89K(6) any reference to an applicable transparency obligation is read subject to section 100A(2)` `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom`

DECLARE `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1) when the requirement takes effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1)(a) immediately`
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1)(b) on the date specified in the notice` HAS `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1) the date specified` IS A DATE

-- src:18240 | (1) A requirement under section 89L takes effect—
-- src:18241 | (a) immediately, if the notice under subsection (2) states that that is the case;
-- src:18242 | (b) in any other case, on such date as may be specified in the notice.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89M(1) Procedure under section 89L: when it takes effect (src:18240-18242)
GIVEN `the notice under subsection (2) states that the requirement takes effect immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1) when the requirement takes effect`
`s 1268 FSMA 89M(1) the requirement under section 89L takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the notice under subsection (2) states that the requirement takes effect immediately`
    THEN `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1)(a) immediately`
    ELSE `s 1268 FSMA 89M(1)(b) on the date specified in the notice` `the date specified in the notice`

-- src:18243 | (2) If the competent authority—
-- src:18244 | (a) proposes to exercise the powers in section 89L in relation to a person, or
-- src:18245 | (b) exercises any of those powers in relation to a person with immediate effect,
-- src:18246 | it must give that person written notice.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89M(2) Procedure under section 89L: written notice (src:18243-18246)
GIVEN `the competent authority proposes to exercise the powers in section 89L in relation to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority exercises any of those powers in relation to a person with immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89M(2) the competent authority must give the person written notice` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority proposes to exercise the powers in section 89L in relation to a person` OR `the competent authority exercises any of those powers in relation to a person with immediate effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the competent authority— (a) proposes to exercise the powers ... or (b) exercises any of those powers ... with immediate effect, it must give that person written notice" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- What the notice must contain (subsection (3)): the terms a notice contains.
DECLARE `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3) notice` HAS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(a) it gives details of the competent authority's action or proposed action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(b) it states the reasons for taking the action and choosing the date on which it took or takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(c) it informs the recipient that he may make representations within such period as is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(d) it informs him of the date on which the action took or takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(e) it informs him of his right to refer the matter to the Tribunal and gives an indication of the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:18247 | (3) The notice must—
-- src:18248 | (a) give details of the competent authority's action or proposed action;
-- src:18249 | (b) state the competent authority's reasons for taking the action in question and choosing the date on which it took effect or takes effect;
-- src:18250 | (c) inform the recipient that he may make representations to the competent authority within such period as may be specified by the notice (whether or not he had referred the matter to the Tribunal);
-- src:18251 | (d) inform him of the date on which the action took effect or takes effect;
-- src:18252 | (e) inform him of his right to refer the matter to the Tribunal (see section 89N) and give an indication of the procedure on such a reference.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89M(3) Procedure under section 89L: what the notice must contain (src:18247-18252)
GIVEN n IS A `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3) notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89M(3) the notice contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       n's `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(a) it gives details of the competent authority's action or proposed action`
         AND n's `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(b) it states the reasons for taking the action and choosing the date on which it took or takes effect`
         AND n's `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(c) it informs the recipient that he may make representations within such period as is specified`
         AND n's `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(d) it informs him of the date on which the action took or takes effect`
         AND n's `s 1268 FSMA 89M(3)(e) it informs him of his right to refer the matter to the Tribunal and gives an indication of the procedure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must— (a) ... (e)" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-D)

-- src:18253 | (4) The competent authority may extend the period within which representations may be made to it.
@ref s 1268 FSMA 89M(4) Procedure under section 89L: extension (src:18253-18253)
GIVEN `the extension is of the period within which representations may be made to the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1268 FSMA 89M(4) the competent authority may extend the period` MEANS
