`s 1268 FSMA 89M(5) the competent authority must give written notice of the decision` MEANS
    IF `having considered any representations made to it, the competent authority decides to maintain, vary or revoke its earlier decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, having considered any representations made to it, the competent authority decides to maintain, vary or revoke its earlier decision, it must give written notice" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:18256 | A person—
-- src:18257 | (a) to whom a decision notice is given under section 89K (public censure), or
