-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1269 Corporate governance rules (FSMA s 89O)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18268 | (2) “Corporate governance”, in relation to an issuer, includes—
-- src:18269 | (a) the nature, constitution or functions of the organs of the issuer;
-- src:18270 | (b) the manner in which organs of the issuer conduct themselves;
-- src:18271 | (c) the requirements imposed on organs of the issuer;
-- src:18272 | (d) the relationship between the different organs of the issuer;
-- src:18273 | (e) the relationship between the organs of the issuer and the members of the issuer or holders of the issuer's securities.
@ref s 1269 FSMA 89O(2) Corporate governance rules: "corporate governance" (src:18268-18273)
GIVEN `the matter is the nature, constitution or functions of the organs of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the manner in which organs of the issuer conduct themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the requirements imposed on organs of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the relationship between the different organs of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the relationship between the organs of the issuer and the members of the issuer or holders of the issuer's securities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1269 FSMA 89O(2) the matter is corporate governance in relation to the issuer` MEANS
    IF       `the matter is the nature, constitution or functions of the organs of the issuer`
          OR `the matter is the manner in which organs of the issuer conduct themselves`
          OR `the matter is the requirements imposed on organs of the issuer`
          OR `the matter is the relationship between the different organs of the issuer`
          OR `the matter is the relationship between the organs of the issuer and the members of the issuer or holders of the issuer's securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Corporate governance”, in relation to an issuer, includes"

-- src:18274 | (3) The burdens and restrictions imposed by rules under this section on foreign-traded issuers must not be greater than the burdens and restrictions imposed on UK-traded issuers by—
-- src:18275 | (a) rules under this section, and
-- src:18276 | (b) listing rules.
@ref s 1269 FSMA 89O(3) Corporate governance rules: foreign-traded issuers (src:18274-18276)
GIVEN `the burden imposed on foreign-traded issuers by rules under section 89O` IS A NUMBER
      `the burden imposed on UK-traded issuers by rules under section 89O and listing rules` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1269 FSMA 89O(3) the burden on foreign-traded issuers is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the burden imposed on foreign-traded issuers by rules under section 89O` GREATER THAN `the burden imposed on UK-traded issuers by rules under section 89O and listing rules`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be greater than the burdens and restrictions imposed on UK-traded issuers"
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the limit named by the function is met; the text does not otherwise say the rules are valid

-- src:18278 | “foreign-traded issuer” means an issuer who has requested or approved admission of the issuer's securities to trading on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom;
@ref s 1269 FSMA 89O(4) Corporate governance rules: "foreign-traded issuer" (src:18278-18278)
GIVEN `the issuer has requested or approved admission of its securities to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulated market is situated or operating outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1269 FSMA 89O(4) the issuer is a foreign-traded issuer` MEANS
    IF `the issuer has requested or approved admission of its securities to trading on a regulated market` AND `the regulated market is situated or operating outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign-traded issuer” means an issuer who has requested or approved admission of the issuer's securities to trading on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom"

-- src:18279 | “UK-traded issuer” means an issuer who has requested or approved admission of the issuer's securities to trading on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1269 FSMA 89O(4) Corporate governance rules: "UK-traded issuer" (src:18279-18279)
GIVEN `the issuer has requested or approved admission of its securities to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulated market is situated or operating in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1269 FSMA 89O(4) the issuer is a UK-traded issuer` MEANS
    IF `the issuer has requested or approved admission of its securities to trading on a regulated market` AND `the regulated market is situated or operating in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK-traded issuer” means an issuer who has requested or approved admission of the issuer's securities to trading on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1270 Liability for false or misleading statements in certain publications (FSMA ss 90A, 90B)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18284 | (1) The publications to which this section applies are—
-- src:18285 | (a) any reports and statements published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive, and
-- src:18286 | (b) any preliminary statement made in advance of a report or statement to be published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4 of that directive, to the extent that it contains information that it is intended—
-- src:18287 | (i) will appear in the report or statement, and
-- src:18288 | (ii) will be presented in the report or statement in substantially the same form as that in which it is presented in the preliminary statement.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(1) Compensation for statements in certain publications: the publications (src:18284-18288)
GIVEN `the report or statement was published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication is a preliminary statement made in advance of a report or statement to be published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4 of that directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the preliminary statement contains information that is intended to appear in the report or statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that information will be presented in the report or statement in substantially the same form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(1) the publication is one to which this section applies` MEANS
    IF       `the report or statement was published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive`
          OR (       `the publication is a preliminary statement made in advance of a report or statement to be published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4 of that directive`
               AND `the preliminary statement contains information that is intended to appear in the report or statement`
               AND `that information will be presented in the report or statement in substantially the same form`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The publications to which this section applies are— (a) ... (b) ..."

-- src:18289 | (2) The securities to which this section applies are—
-- src:18290 | (a) securities that are traded on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:18291 | (b) securities that—
-- src:18292 | (i) are traded on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:18293 | (ii) are issued by an issuer for which the United Kingdom is the home Member State within the meaning of Article 2.1(i) of the transparency obligations directive.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(2) Compensation for statements in certain publications: the securities (src:18289-18293)
GIVEN `the securities are traded on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities are traded on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities are issued by an issuer for which the United Kingdom is the home Member State within the meaning of Article 2.1(i) of the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(2) the securities are ones to which this section applies` MEANS
    IF       `the securities are traded on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom`
          OR (`the securities are traded on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom`
              AND `the securities are issued by an issuer for which the United Kingdom is the home Member State within the meaning of Article 2.1(i) of the transparency obligations directive`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The securities to which this section applies are— (a) ... (b) ..."

-- src:18294 | (3) The issuer of securities to which this section applies is liable to pay compensation to a person who has—
-- src:18295 | (a) acquired such securities issued by it, and
-- src:18296 | (b) suffered loss in respect of them as a result of—
-- src:18297 | (i) any untrue or misleading statement in a publication to which this section applies, or
-- src:18298 | (ii) the omission from any such publication of any matter required to be included in it.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(3) Compensation for statements in certain publications: the issuer's liability (src:18294-18298)
GIVEN `the securities are ones to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has acquired such securities issued by the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has suffered loss in respect of them as a result of an untrue or misleading statement in a publication to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has suffered loss in respect of them as a result of the omission from such a publication of a matter required to be included in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(3) the issuer is liable to pay compensation to the person` MEANS
    IF       `the securities are ones to which this section applies`
         AND `the person has acquired such securities issued by the issuer`
         AND (`the person has suffered loss in respect of them as a result of an untrue or misleading statement in a publication to which this section applies`
              OR `the person has suffered loss in respect of them as a result of the omission from such a publication of a matter required to be included in it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- subject to the limits in subsections (4) and (5), which the next two functions answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who has (a) acquired such securities issued by it, and (b) suffered loss in respect of them as a result of"

-- src:18299 | (4) The issuer is so liable only if a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication—
-- src:18300 | (a) knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading, or
-- src:18301 | (b) knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(4) Compensation for statements in certain publications: the knowledge limit (src:18299-18301)
GIVEN `a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(4) the limit on the issuer's liability is satisfied` MEANS
    IF       `a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading`
          OR `a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The issuer is so liable only if a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:18302 | (5) A loss is not regarded as suffered as a result of the statement or omission in the publication unless the person suffering it acquired the relevant securities—
-- src:18303 | (a) in reliance on the information in the publication, and
-- src:18304 | (b) at a time when, and in circumstances in which, it was reasonable for him to rely on that information.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(5) Compensation for statements in certain publications: reliance (src:18302-18304)
GIVEN `the person acquired the relevant securities in reliance on the information in the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at that time, and in those circumstances, it was reasonable for him to rely on that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(5) the loss is regarded as suffered as a result of the statement or omission` MEANS
    IF `the person acquired the relevant securities in reliance on the information in the publication` AND `at that time, and in those circumstances, it was reasonable for him to rely on that information`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the limit in subsection (5) is met; the loss still has to be one in subsection (3)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A loss is not regarded as suffered as a result of the statement or omission in the publication unless the person suffering it acquired the relevant securities— (a) in reliance on the information in the publication, and (b) at a time when, and in circumstances in which, it was reasonable for him to rely on that information"

-- src:18294 | (3) The issuer of securities to which this section applies is liable to pay compensation to a person who has—
-- src:18295 | (a) acquired such securities issued by it, and
-- src:18296 | (b) suffered loss in respect of them as a result of—
-- src:18297 | (i) any untrue or misleading statement in a publication to which this section applies, or
-- src:18298 | (ii) the omission from any such publication of any matter required to be included in it.
-- src:18299 | (4) The issuer is so liable only if a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication—
-- src:18300 | (a) knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading, or
-- src:18301 | (b) knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact.
-- src:18302 | (5) A loss is not regarded as suffered as a result of the statement or omission in the publication unless the person suffering it acquired the relevant securities—
-- src:18303 | (a) in reliance on the information in the publication, and
-- src:18304 | (b) at a time when, and in circumstances in which, it was reasonable for him to rely on that information.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(3)-(5) Compensation for statements in certain publications: liability, with its limits (src:18294-18304)
GIVEN `the issuer is liable under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the limit in subsection (4) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the loss is regarded as suffered as a result under subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(3)-(5) the issuer is liable to pay compensation` MEANS
    IF (`the limit in subsection (4) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the loss is regarded as suffered as a result under subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (4), "so liable only if"; subsection (5), "not regarded as suffered ... unless"
    ELSE IF       `the issuer is liable under subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the limit in subsection (4) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the loss is regarded as suffered as a result under subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) does not reach the case, or one of the three answers is not covered

-- src:18315 | (9) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:18316 | (a) the following are persons “discharging managerial responsibilities” in relation to a publication—
-- src:18317 | (i) any director of the issuer (or person occupying the position of director, by whatever name called),
-- src:18318 | (ii) in the case of an issuer whose affairs are managed by its members, any member of the issuer,
-- src:18319 | (iii) in the case of an issuer that has no persons within sub-paragraph (i) or (ii), any senior executive of the issuer having responsibilities in relation to the publication;
-- src:18320 | (b) references to the acquisition by a person of securities include his contracting to acquire them or any interest in them.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(9) Compensation for statements in certain publications: managerial responsibilities (src:18315-18320)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the issuer or occupies the position of director, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer's affairs are managed by its members and the person is a member of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer has no persons within sub-paragraph (i) or (ii) and the person is a senior executive of the issuer having responsibilities in relation to the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(9)(a) the person is a person discharging managerial responsibilities in relation to the publication` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a director of the issuer or occupies the position of director, by whatever name called`
          OR `the issuer's affairs are managed by its members and the person is a member of the issuer`
          OR `the issuer has no persons within sub-paragraph (i) or (ii) and the person is a senior executive of the issuer having responsibilities in relation to the publication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following are persons “discharging managerial responsibilities” in relation to a publication" and the text does not say there are no others

@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(9)(b) Compensation for statements in certain publications: acquisition (src:18320-18320)
GIVEN `the person acquired the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contracted to acquire the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contracted to acquire an interest in the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(9)(b) the person has acquired securities` MEANS
    IF `the person acquired the securities` OR `the person contracted to acquire the securities` OR `the person contracted to acquire an interest in the securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the acquisition by a person of securities include his contracting to acquire them or any interest in them"

-- src:18305 | (6) Except as mentioned in subsection (8)—
-- src:18306 | (a) the issuer is not subject to any other liability than that provided for by this section in respect of loss suffered as a result of reliance by any person on—
-- src:18307 | (i) an untrue or misleading statement in a publication to which this section applies, or
-- src:18308 | (ii) the omission from any such publication of any matter required to be included in it, and
-- src:18309 | (b) a person other than the issuer is not subject to any liability, other than to the issuer, in respect of any such loss.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(6) Compensation for statements in certain publications: no other liability (src:18305-18309)
GIVEN `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one mentioned in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(6)(a) the issuer is subject to a liability other than that provided for by this section` MEANS
    IF `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which this section applies` AND (NOT `the liability is one mentioned in subsection (8)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the issuer is not subject to any other liability than that provided for by this section in respect of loss suffered as a result of reliance"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as mentioned in subsection (8)"; and only for loss suffered as a result of reliance on such a publication

@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(6) Compensation for statements in certain publications: no liability of others (src:18305-18309)
GIVEN `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is to the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one mentioned in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(6)(b) a person other than the issuer is subject to a liability` MEANS
    IF       `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which this section applies`
         AND (NOT `the liability is to the issuer`)
         AND (NOT `the liability is one mentioned in subsection (8)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person other than the issuer is not subject to any liability, other than to the issuer, in respect of any such loss"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as mentioned in subsection (8)"; and only for such loss

-- src:18310 | (7) Any reference in subsection (6) to a person being subject to a liability includes a reference to another person being entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(7) Compensation for statements in certain publications: "subject to a liability" (src:18310-18310)
GIVEN `another person is entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person is entitled as against him to rescind or repudiate an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(7) he is subject to a liability` MEANS
    IF `another person is entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy` OR `another person is entitled as against him to rescind or repudiate an agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a person being subject to a liability includes a reference to another person being entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement"

DECLARE `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8)(a) the powers conferred by sections 382 and 384 (restitution orders of the court and requirements of the Authority)`
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8)(b) liability for a civil penalty`
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8)(c) liability for a criminal offence`
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) another matter`

-- src:18311 | (8) This section does not affect—
-- src:18312 | (a) the powers conferred by section 382 and 384 (powers of the court to make a restitution order and of the Authority to require restitution);
-- src:18313 | (b) liability for a civil penalty;
-- src:18314 | (c) liability for a criminal offence.
@ref s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) Compensation for statements in certain publications: matters not affected (src:18311-18314)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) this section affects the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 1270 FSMA 90A(8) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the list is of what the section "does not affect" and says nothing of other matters
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1271 Exercise of powers where UK is host member State (FSMA s 100A)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18327 | (1) This section applies to the exercise by the competent authority of any power under this Part exercisable in case of infringement of—
-- src:18328 | (a) a provision of prospectus rules or any other provision made in accordance with the prospectus directive, or
-- src:18329 | (b) a provision of transparency rules or any other provision made in accordance with the transparency obligations directive,
-- src:18330 | in relation to an issuer whose home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(1) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: scope (src:18327-18330)
GIVEN `the competent authority is exercising a power under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 exercisable in case of infringement of a provision of prospectus rules or transparency rules, or of any other provision made in accordance with the prospectus directive or the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority is exercising a power under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 exercisable in case of infringement of a provision of prospectus rules or transparency rules, or of any other provision made in accordance with the prospectus directive or the transparency obligations directive`
       AND `the issuer's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to the exercise by the competent authority of any power under this Part ... in relation to an issuer whose home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom"

-- src:18331 | (2) The competent authority may act in such a case only in respect of the infringement of a provision required by the relevant directive.
-- src:18332 | Any reference to an applicable provision or applicable transparency obligation shall be read accordingly.
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(2) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: only for provisions required by the directive (src:18331-18332)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the infringement is of a provision required by the relevant directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(2) the competent authority may act` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1)
    ELSE IF `the infringement is of a provision required by the relevant directive`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The competent authority may act in such a case only in respect of the infringement of a provision required by the relevant directive"

@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(2) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: read accordingly (src:18332-18332)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is a provision required by the relevant directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(2) the provision is an applicable provision or applicable transparency obligation` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1)
    ELSE IF `the provision is a provision required by the relevant directive`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any reference to an applicable provision or applicable transparency obligation shall be read accordingly" (that is, as limited to a provision required by the relevant directive)

-- src:18333 | (3) If the authority finds that there has been such an infringement, it must give a notice to that effect to the competent authority of the person's home State requesting it—
-- src:18334 | (a) to take all appropriate measures for the purpose of ensuring that the person remedies the situation that has given rise to the notice, and
-- src:18335 | (b) to inform the authority of the measures it proposes to take or has taken or the reasons for not taking such measures.
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(3) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: the notice to the home State's authority (src:18333-18335)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority finds that there has been such an infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(3) the authority must give a notice to the competent authority of the person's home State` MEANS
    IF `this section applies` AND `the authority finds that there has been such an infringement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the authority finds that there has been such an infringement, it must give a notice" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:18336 | (4) The authority may not act further unless satisfied—
-- src:18337 | (a) that the competent authority of the person's home State has failed or refused to take measures for the purpose mentioned in subsection (3)(a), or
-- src:18338 | (b) that the measures taken by that authority have proved inadequate for that purpose.
-- src:18339 | This does not affect exercise of the powers under section 87K(2), 87L(2) or (3) or 89L(2) or (3) (powers to protect market).
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(4) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: acting further (src:18336-18339)
GIVEN `the authority is satisfied that the competent authority of the person's home State has failed or refused to take measures for the purpose mentioned in subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is satisfied that the measures taken by that authority have proved inadequate for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(4) the authority may act further` MEANS
    IF `the authority is satisfied that the competent authority of the person's home State has failed or refused to take measures for the purpose mentioned in subsection (3)(a)` OR `the authority is satisfied that the measures taken by that authority have proved inadequate for that purpose`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may not act further unless satisfied" makes satisfaction a necessary condition and does not say it is enough
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authority may not act further unless satisfied"

-- src:18339 | This does not affect exercise of the powers under section 87K(2), 87L(2) or (3) or 89L(2) or (3) (powers to protect market).
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(4) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: powers to protect the market (src:18339-18339)
GIVEN `the power is one under section 87K(2), 87L(2) or (3) or 89L(2) or (3) (powers to protect market)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(4) the restriction affects the exercise of the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is one under section 87K(2), 87L(2) or (3) or 89L(2) or (3) (powers to protect market)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not affect exercise of the powers under section 87K(2), 87L(2) or (3) or 89L(2) or (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the powers it does not affect

-- src:18340 | (5) If the authority is so satisfied, it must, after informing the competent authority of the person's home State, take all appropriate measures to protect investors.
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(5) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: measures to protect investors (src:18340-18340)
GIVEN `the authority is so satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(5) the authority must take all appropriate measures to protect investors` MEANS
    IF `the authority is so satisfied`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- after informing the competent authority of the person's home State
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the authority is so satisfied, it must, after informing the competent authority of the person's home State, take all appropriate measures" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:18341 | (6) In such a case the authority must inform the Commission of the measures at the earliest opportunity..
@ref s 1271 FSMA 100A(6) Exercise of powers where UK is host member State: informing the Commission (src:18341-18341)
GIVEN `the authority has taken measures under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1271 FSMA 100A(6) the authority must inform the Commission of the measures at the earliest opportunity` MEANS
    IF `the authority has taken measures under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case the authority must inform the Commission of the measures"
